Z||000005||Raydar||11-04-1999||08:12 PM||||Just a thought...I wouldn't recommend using just resonator tips. I set up my V-6 like this (cat, stainless pipes, resonators), and it was just *damn loud*. Sounded like an airplane. The "thrum" that you heard (and felt) with the windows down was most unpleasant. Even set off car alarms in our parking garage at work. Stock muffler sounded *much* better. ||||reg||11
Z||000006||Phil||11-04-1999||08:36 PM||||I had the same problem setting up an exhaust system after an engine swap (no room for a muffler) wound up using Hooker Exhaust tips. They still have a good rumble but are definately quieter than the resonator tips .They are 10" long 2 1/4" inlet||||reg||1
